      <div>
        <h2>A risk present across every medical coverage assignment you run</h2>
        <p class="partner-section__lead">Exertional heat stroke (EHS) affects the public you're responsible for, whatever type of assignment it is. At a parade or a street festival, that's people on the move, sometimes for several hours, under continuous exertion in the heat. At a music festival or fireworks display, that's a dense crowd, often standing and largely stationary, exposed to heat for the full length of the event.</p>
        <p class="partner-section__lead">For a complete breakdown of the physiological mechanisms and warning signs, read our <a href="https://kollder.com/blog/en/2026-06-04-exertional-heat-stroke-recognise-and-treat/" class="inline-link">guide to exertional heat stroke</a> and our guide on <a href="https://kollder.com/blog/en/2026-07-09-climate-change-rising-frequency-heat-waves/" class="inline-link">preparing first responder teams</a> for more frequent extreme heat events.</p>
      </div>
