        <p class="partner-section__lead">At a festival, parade, or fireworks display, a tarp held by several volunteers and filled with water remains a common way to treat a victim in hyperthermia. It works, but it ties up several people just to hold the tarp, takes time to set up in a dense crowd, and limits access to the victim for monitoring.</p>
        <p class="partner-section__lead">Our <a href="https://kollder.com/blog/en/2026-06-04-cooling-solutions-exertional-heat-stroke-field-comparison/" class="inline-link">comparison of cooling methods</a> breaks down the performance gaps. For associations equipping multiple first aid posts, two objective comparisons are also available: <a href="https://kollder.com/blog/en/2026-05-25-kollder-vs-corben-emergency-cooling-tub-comparison/" class="inline-link">Kollder vs. Corben</a> and <a href="https://kollder.com/blog/en/2026-05-25-kollder-vs-icwik-cold-water-immersion-comparison/" class="inline-link">Kollder vs. I-CWIK</a>.</p>
